 75	/// The one place this app ever decides a card's badge (Never: "any screen
 76	/// recomputing badge state inline") — pure, no I/O, no `package:flutter`
 77	/// import (RNF06).
 78	///
 79	/// [pending] wins whenever it's non-null, regardless of [entry] — per
 80	/// `sync-badge.md`, "Synchronizing"/"Synchronization error" both describe
 81	/// *client-side pending state*, not anything read off [entry] itself, so a
 82	/// pending write's own status is always the authoritative answer for
 83	/// whichever card it belongs to. Once [pending] is `null`, the existence of
 84	/// a confirmed [entry] already means "it is on the server" (sync-
 85	/// badge.md: "it is on the server already means synchronized, by
 86	/// definition") -> [SyncBadgeSynchronized]. [entry] and [pending] both
 87	/// `null` is unreachable from every real caller (`MeusRegistrosLoaded`
 88	/// always derives a displayed card from one or the other, never neither)
 89	/// but still resolves to [SyncBadgeSynchronized] rather than throwing
 90	/// (RNF09-style defensiveness) — "nothing pending" is the closest true
 91	/// reading of that combination regardless of [entry].
 92	SyncBadgeState deriveSyncBadgeState(Entry? entry, PendingEntryWrite? pending) {
 93	  if (pending != null) {
 94	    return switch (pending.status) {
 95	      PendingEntryWriteInFlight() => const SyncBadgeState.synchronizing(),
 96	      PendingEntryWriteFailed(failure: final failure) => SyncBadgeState.error(
 97	        failure,
 98	      ),
 99	    };
100	  }
101	  return const SyncBadgeState.synchronized();
102	}

